            "markdown": {
              "en": "# China · K3 · Lesson 2\n## Paper, Silk and Porcelain\n\n## 1. Lesson Identity\n\n- Country / Place: China\n- Grade: K3\n- Lesson: 2 of 4\n\n## 2. Lesson Focus\n\nChildren explore Chinese making through materials and patterns. They compare paper, silk-like fabric, and porcelain-style surfaces, then create simple prints, rubbings, or blue-and-white pattern designs.\n\n## 3. Learning Objectives\n\nChildren will:\n\n- notice different material qualities such as soft, smooth, thin, hard, light, or strong;\n- explore paper, fabric, and porcelain-style visual patterns;\n- use printing, rubbing, folding, or pattern-making to create a simple design and describe one material they used.\n\n## 4. Teacher Language\n\nTeacher Input:\n\n- Touch the paper. How does it feel?\n- This fabric is soft.\n- This plate is smooth.\n- Look at the blue and white pattern.\n- Let’s make a pattern.\n- Press and print.\n- Fold the paper.\n- Which material do you want to use?\n- What did you make?\n- Tell us about your design.\n\nPossible Child Response:\n\n- It is soft / smooth / hard / thin.\n- I choose paper.\n- I made a pattern.\n- I used blue.\n- This is my plate.\n- I printed flowers / lines / waves.\n- I like this design.\n\n## 5. Suggested Games and Activities\n\n### Activity 1: Material Touch and Sort\n\n**Purpose:**  \nHelp children observe and compare materials before making.\n\n**Materials:**  \nPaper samples, cardboard, tissue paper, silk-like fabric or scarves, smooth ceramic-safe objects or porcelain-style images, trays, sorting mats, and label cards such as soft, smooth, rough, thin, strong.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare safe samples in small baskets. Avoid breakable real porcelain unless handled only by the teacher. Use images or plastic/ceramic-safe substitutes when needed.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren touch and compare materials. They sort them by feel or use: writing, wrapping, wearing, decorating, building, or eating from. The teacher prompts children to justify simple choices.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nKeep the language concrete. K3 children can handle comparison language, but the activity should remain sensory and practical.\n\n### Activity 2: Blue-and-White Pattern Studio\n\n**Purpose:**  \nLet children create a visual design inspired by blue-and-white porcelain patterns.\n\n**Materials:**  \nPaper plates or circular cardstock, blue markers or paint, pattern reference cards, stamps, rollers, cotton swabs, and pencils.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare pattern examples with simple motifs: dots, waves, flowers, lines, circles, borders. Avoid overly detailed designs that frustrate children.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren look at several blue-and-white pattern images and notice repeated lines, dots, flowers, or waves. They design their own paper plate using repeated marks and borders.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nFrame this as pattern exploration, not copying. Children should make a design they can explain, such as “I used dots around the edge” or “I made waves.”\n\n### Activity 3: Print, Rub, Fold\n\n**Purpose:**  \nConnect paper with making processes.\n\n**Materials:**  \nPaper, textured rubbing plates or leaves, crayons, stamps, ink pads or paint trays, simple folding paper, and drying space.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nSet up three small stations: rubbing, printing, and folding. Keep instructions visual and short.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren rotate through stations or choose one. They make a rubbing, create repeated prints, or fold paper into a simple shape. At the end, they place one piece on a “Made with Paper” display.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nDo not present paper-making, silk, and porcelain as an information-heavy invention list. The lesson should stay focused on touching, comparing, making, and explaining.",
              "zh": "# 中国 · K3 · 第 2 课\n## 纸、丝绸与瓷器\n\n## 1. 课程身份\n\n- 国家 / 地区：中国\n- 年级：K3\n- 课次：4 课中的第 2 课\n\n## 2. 课程重点\n\n幼儿通过材料和花样的视角来探索中国的\"造物\"传统。他们比较纸、丝绸感的布和瓷器感的光滑表面，然后做简单的印刷、拓印或青花图案设计。\n\n## 3. 学习目标\n\n幼儿将：\n\n- 注意不同的材料质感：软、光滑、薄、硬、轻或结实；\n- 探索纸、布和瓷器感的视觉花样的不同；\n- 用印刷、拓印、折纸或图案设计做一个简单的设计，并描述自己用的那种材料。\n\n## 4. 教师语言\n\n教师输入：\n\n- Touch the paper. How does it feel?\n- This fabric is soft.\n- This plate is smooth.\n- Look at the blue and white pattern.\n- Let’s make a pattern.\n- Press and print.\n- Fold the paper.\n- Which material do you want to use?\n- What did you make?\n- Tell us about your design.\n\n幼儿可能回应：\n\n- It is soft / smooth / hard / thin.\n- I choose paper.\n- I made a pattern.\n- I used blue.\n- This is my plate.\n- I printed flowers / lines / waves.\n- I like this design.\n\n## 5. 建议游戏与活动\n\n### 活动 1：摸一摸，分一分\n\n**目的：**\n在动手之前，先让幼儿观察和比较不同材料。\n\n**材料：**\n纸样、纸板、餐巾纸、丝绸感的布或围巾、安全的陶瓷感物品或瓷器图片、托盘、分类垫，以及标签卡：软、光滑、粗糙、薄、结实。\n\n**准备：**\n把安全的样本装到小篮子里。除非只在教师手里操作，否则不要用真正易碎的瓷器。必要时用图片或塑料 / 安全替代物。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿摸一摸、比较各种材料。按触感或用途来分：写字、包东西、穿、装饰、搭建、盛食物。教师提示幼儿说出简单的理由。\n\n**教师提示：**\n语言保持具体。K3 幼儿可以做\"比较\"层面的表达，但活动整体仍然要\"摸得到、做得来\"。\n\n### 活动 2：青花图案工作室\n\n**目的：**\n让幼儿做一个受青花瓷图案启发的视觉设计。\n\n**材料：**\n纸盘或圆形卡纸、蓝色马克笔或颜料、图案参考卡、印章、滚筒、棉签、铅笔。\n\n**准备：**\n准备几张简单纹样的参考：点、波浪、花、线条、圆、边纹。避免太复杂让幼儿受挫的设计。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿看几张青花图案图片，注意其中反复出现的线、点、花、波浪。然后在纸盘上用重复的图案和边纹设计自己的盘子。\n\n**教师提示：**\n把它定位为\"图案探索\"，不是\"照着画\"。让幼儿做出一个能讲出来的设计，比如\"我在边上画了圆点\"或\"我画了波浪\"。\n\n### 活动 3：印一印、拓一拓、折一折\n\n**目的：**\n把\"纸\"和\"做\"的过程连起来。\n\n**材料：**\n纸、有凹凸纹样的拓印板或叶子、蜡笔、印章、印台或颜料盘、简单的折纸、晾干空间。\n\n**准备：**\n布置三个小站：拓印、印刷、折纸。每站用图示 + 简短文字呈现做法。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿轮换站点，或者自己选一个站。做一张拓印、做一组重复的印刷、或者把纸折成简单的形状。最后把自己的作品贴到一面\"用纸做的\"展示墙上。\n\n**教师提示：**\n不要把\"造纸、丝绸、瓷器\"讲成一份沉重的\"发明清单\"课。重点仍然是摸、比较、做、说。"
            }
