            "number": 2,
            "markdown": {
              "en": "# USA · K1 · Lesson 2\n## USA Food and Everyday Pop Culture\n\n## 1. Lesson Identity\n\n- Country / Place: USA\n- Grade: K1\n- Lesson: 2 of 4\n\n## 2. Lesson Focus\n\nChildren explore familiar USA-related food and everyday pop-culture images through pretend play, matching, sorting, and simple choice-making.\n\n## 3. Learning Objectives\n\nChildren will:\n- recognise or explore familiar food items linked with USA popular culture;\n- sort, choose, set, or pretend with food props;\n- connect food, pictures, and simple social routines through playful exploration without needing to explain brands or cultural history.\n\n## 4. Teacher Language\n\nTeacher Input:\n- Look at the food.\n- This is a hamburger.\n- This is popcorn.\n- Do you like it?\n- I like hamburgers.\n- Put it on the plate.\n- Here you are.\n- Thank you.\n\nPossible Child Response:\n- hamburger\n- popcorn\n- fries\n- drink\n- I like it.\n- Here you are.\n- Thank you.\n\n## 5. Suggested Games and Activities\n\n### Activity 1: USA Food Basket Sort\n\n**Purpose:**  \nHelp children recognise and sort familiar food props.\n\n**Materials:**  \nToy food or picture cards: hamburger, fries, hot dog, popcorn, drink cup, apple or other contrast foods; baskets or trays.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare two or three baskets: “food,” “drink,” and “not today” or “I like.” Use pictures if toy food is not available.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nShow one food item at a time and invite children to place it into a basket. Keep the sorting rule very simple: food/drink, big/small, or I like/I don’t like. Repeat the names naturally without requiring full sentences.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nThis is not a nutrition lesson and not a brand lesson. Keep the focus on familiar food objects, choosing, sorting, and pretend play.\n\n### Activity 2: Popcorn Cinema Corner\n\n**Purpose:**  \nUse popcorn and cinema-style play to introduce a child-friendly pop-culture setting.\n\n**Materials:**  \nPopcorn picture cards or paper popcorn crafts, paper cups, pretend tickets, chairs arranged like a small cinema, short silent cartoon or image slideshow if appropriate.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nSet up a small “cinema” area. Prepare simple tickets and cups.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren take a ticket, sit in the cinema corner, and receive a paper popcorn cup. The teacher models: “Ticket, please,” “Here you are,” “Thank you,” and “Popcorn.” Children watch a very short visual clip or look at a slideshow of USA pop-culture-style images such as cartoons, sports, or city scenes.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nKeep screen time short if used. The main experience is role play and routine language, not watching a long video.\n\n### Activity 3: Hamburger Shop Role Play\n\n**Purpose:**  \nLet children connect USA food elements with social interaction and pretend service routines.\n\n**Materials:**  \nToy hamburgers or paper hamburger parts, plates, trays, simple shop sign, pretend money if desired.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare a small table as a hamburger shop. Place food items in baskets.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren take turns being shop helper and customer. The helper gives a hamburger, fries, or drink. The teacher models short exchanges: “A hamburger, please,” “Here you are,” “Thank you.” Children can also build a paper hamburger by stacking bun, lettuce, cheese, and patty shapes.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nUse commercial brand images carefully. If shown, frame them as examples of familiar pop-culture symbols, not advertising.",
              "zh": "# 美国 · K1 · 第 2 课\n## 美国食物和日常生活中的流行文化\n\n## 1. 课程身份\n\n- 国家 / 地区：美国\n- 年级：K1\n- 课次：4 课中的第 2 课\n\n## 2. 课程重点\n\n幼儿通过假装游戏、匹配、分类和简单的选择，认识熟悉的美国相关食物和日常生活中的流行文化图像。\n\n## 3. 学习目标\n\n幼儿将：\n\n- 认出或探索与美国流行文化有关的熟悉食物；\n- 用分类、选择、摆放或假装游戏的方式操作食物道具；\n- 通过游戏化探索把食物、图片和简单的社交常规连起来，不需要解释品牌或文化历史。\n\n## 4. 教师语言\n\n教师输入：\n\n- Look at the food.\n- This is a hamburger.\n- This is popcorn.\n- Do you like it?\n- I like hamburgers.\n- Put it on the plate.\n- Here you are.\n- Thank you.\n\n幼儿可能回应：\n\n- hamburger\n- popcorn\n- fries\n- drink\n- I like it.\n- Here you are.\n- Thank you.\n\n## 5. 建议游戏与活动\n\n### 活动 1：美国食物篮分类\n\n**目的：**\n帮助幼儿认出并分类熟悉的食物道具。\n\n**材料：**\n玩具食物或图片卡：汉堡、薯条、热狗、爆米花、饮料杯、苹果或其他对比类食物；篮子或托盘。\n\n**准备：**\n准备两到三个篮子，比如\"食物\"\"饮料\"\"今天不吃\"或\"我喜欢\"。如果没有玩具食物，用图片也可以。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n教师一次出示一种食物，请幼儿把它放到一个篮子里。分类规则保持非常简单：食物 / 饮料、大 / 小、喜欢 / 不喜欢。重复说出食物名字，但不要求幼儿说完整句子。\n\n**教师提示：**\n这既不是营养课，也不是品牌课。重点放在熟悉的食物、选择、分类和假装游戏。\n\n### 活动 2：爆米花小影院\n\n**目的：**\n用爆米花和影院式游戏，引入一个适合幼儿的流行文化场景。\n\n**材料：**\n爆米花图片卡或纸做的爆米花、纸杯、仿真电影票、摆成小影院的几把椅子；如有合适内容，可以准备一段很短的无声卡通或图片幻灯片。\n\n**准备：**\n布置一个小的\"影院\"区。准备简单的票和杯子。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿拿票、坐进影院区、领一纸杯\"爆米花\"。教师示范：\"Ticket, please\"\"Here you are\"\"Thank you\"\"Popcorn\"。幼儿看一段很短的画面，或一起看一组美国流行文化风格图片，比如卡通、运动或城市场景。\n\n**教师提示：**\n如果用屏幕，时间要很短。重点是角色扮演和常规语言，不是看一段长视频。\n\n### 活动 3：汉堡店角色扮演\n\n**目的：**\n让幼儿把美国食物元素和社交互动、假装服务常规连起来。\n\n**材料：**\n玩具汉堡或纸做的汉堡组件、盘子、托盘、简单的店招、如果方便可以加仿真钱币。\n\n**准备：**\n用一张小桌子布置一个汉堡店。把食物放在几个篮子里。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿轮流当\"店员\"和\"顾客\"。店员递一个汉堡、薯条或饮料。教师示范简单对话：\"A hamburger, please\"\"Here you are\"\"Thank you\"。幼儿也可以把面包片、生菜、奶酪、肉饼等形状叠起来，做一个纸汉堡。\n\n**教师提示：**\n用商业品牌图像时要谨慎。如果展示，要把它们当作\"常见的流行文化符号的例子\"，而不是广告。"
            }
