            "markdown": {
              "en": "# USA · K2 · Lesson 2\n## Food, Sports, and Everyday Life\n\n## 1. Lesson Identity\n\n- Country / Place: USA\n- Grade: K2\n- Lesson: 2 of 4\n\n## 2. Lesson Focus\n\nChildren explore familiar USA-related food and sports by sorting, matching, comparing, and joining simple role play.\n\n## 3. Learning Objectives\n\nChildren will:\n- identify familiar food and sport elements linked with USA popular culture;\n- sort food and sport images by simple features;\n- match sports with equipment or actions and express simple preferences through words, gestures, or short phrases.\n\n## 4. Teacher Language\n\nTeacher Input:\n- What food can you see?\n- Do you like hamburgers?\n- Put the food here.\n- Put the sports here.\n- This is basketball.\n- What do we need for baseball?\n- Same or different?\n- Which one do you like?\n\nPossible Child Response:\n- hamburger / popcorn / fries\n- basketball / baseball\n- I like basketball.\n- I like hamburgers.\n- food / sport\n- same / different\n\n## 5. Suggested Games and Activities\n\n### Activity 1: Food or Sport?\n\n**Purpose:**  \nHelp children sort familiar USA-related images into meaningful groups.\n\n**Materials:**  \nFood cards: hamburger, fries, hot dog, popcorn, drink. Sport cards: basketball, baseball, football, ball, bat, hoop.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare two large sorting mats: Food and Sports. Use icons to support non-readers.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren take turns choosing a card and placing it on the correct mat. After each placement, the teacher asks a simple follow-up: “Do you like it?” “Can you play it?” “Is it food?”\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nKeep American football optional; basketball and baseball are easier for children to understand and act out.\n\n### Activity 2: USA Snack Shop\n\n**Purpose:**  \nUse food props for social role play, choosing, and preference language.\n\n**Materials:**  \nToy food or paper food props, trays, plates, cups, shop sign, optional pretend menu with pictures.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nSet up a small snack shop with two or three food choices.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren choose food from a picture menu and place it on a tray. The teacher models: “A hamburger, please,” “Here you are,” “Thank you,” “I like popcorn.” Children can take turns being helper and customer.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nThis is pretend play, not an eating activity. If real food is used, check school policies and allergies first.\n\n### Activity 3: Basketball and Baseball Actions\n\n**Purpose:**  \nConnect USA sports with movement, action words, and simple equipment matching.\n\n**Materials:**  \nSoft balls, hoop or basket, bat picture, baseball glove picture, sport cards, cones.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nSet up a safe movement area. Use soft balls only.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nShow sport cards and act out simple movements: bounce, throw, catch, hit, run. Children match a sport card with an action or object. Then they try a simple basketball throw or baseball-style pretend swing without hard equipment.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nPrioritise safety and turn-taking. Keep the activity about movement and recognition, not sport skill training.",
              "zh": "# 美国 · K2 · 第 2 课\n## 食物、运动和日常生活\n\n## 1. 课程身份\n\n- 国家 / 地区：美国\n- 年级：K2\n- 课次：4 课中的第 2 课\n\n## 2. 课程重点\n\n幼儿通过分类、匹配、比较和简单的角色扮演，认识熟悉的美国相关食物和运动。\n\n## 3. 学习目标\n\n幼儿将：\n\n- 识别与美国流行文化有关的食物和运动元素；\n- 按简单特征给食物和运动图片分类；\n- 把运动和器材或动作匹配，并用词、手势或短句表达简单的偏好。\n\n## 4. 教师语言\n\n教师输入：\n\n- What food can you see?\n- Do you like hamburgers?\n- Put the food here.\n- Put the sports here.\n- This is basketball.\n- What do we need for baseball?\n- Same or different?\n- Which one do you like?\n\n幼儿可能回应：\n\n- hamburger / popcorn / fries\n- basketball / baseball\n- I like basketball.\n- I like hamburgers.\n- food / sport\n- same / different\n\n## 5. 建议游戏与活动\n\n### 活动 1：食物还是运动？\n\n**目的：**\n帮助幼儿把熟悉的美国相关图片分成有意义的组。\n\n**材料：**\n食物卡：汉堡、薯条、热狗、爆米花、饮料。运动卡：篮球、棒球、橄榄球、球、球棒、篮筐。\n\n**准备：**\n准备两张大的分类垫：食物、运动。用图标帮助不识字的幼儿。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿轮流选一张卡，放到正确的垫上。每次放完，教师问一个简单追问：\"Do you like it?\"\"Can you play it?\"\"Is it food?\"。\n\n**教师提示：**\n美式橄榄球可以选做；篮球和棒球对幼儿更容易理解，也更容易演一演。\n\n### 活动 2：美国小食店\n\n**目的：**\n用食物道具做社交角色扮演、选择和表达偏好。\n\n**材料：**\n玩具食物或纸做的食物、托盘、盘子、杯子、店招、可以加一个带图片的仿真菜单。\n\n**准备：**\n布置一个有两到三种食物选择的小食店。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿从图片菜单上选一种食物，放到托盘上。教师示范：\"A hamburger, please\"\"Here you are\"\"Thank you\"\"I like popcorn\"。幼儿可以轮流当\"店员\"和\"顾客\"。\n\n**教师提示：**\n这是角色扮演，不是真吃。如果用真食物，要先确认学校政策和过敏情况。\n\n### 活动 3：篮球和棒球动作\n\n**目的：**\n把美国运动和动作、动作词、简单的器材匹配连起来。\n\n**材料：**\n软球、篮筐或球框、棒球棒图片、棒球手套图片、运动卡、锥形桶。\n\n**准备：**\n布置一个安全的活动区。只用软球。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n出示运动卡，演一些简单动作：拍、扔、接、打、跑。幼儿把运动卡和动作或物品匹配起来。然后做一次简单的篮球投掷或棒球式的假装挥棒，不使用硬器材。\n\n**教师提示：**\n安全和轮流第一。重点是\"动起来\"和\"认出来\"，不是运动技能训练。"
            }
