            "number": 2,
            "markdown": {
              "en": "# USA · K3 · Lesson 2\n## USA Icons — Food, Sports and Popular Culture\n\n## 1. Lesson Identity\n\n- Country / Place: USA\n- Grade: K3\n- Lesson: 2 of 4\n\n## 2. Lesson Focus\n\nChildren investigate familiar USA icons from food, sports, film, cartoons, and everyday visual culture, then discuss why some images become widely recognised.\n\n## 3. Learning Objectives\n\nChildren will:\n- identify familiar USA-linked food, sport, and pop-culture images;\n- organise icons by category and function;\n- compare what feels familiar and what feels new, then select one icon for a USA guide or museum display.\n\n## 4. Teacher Language\n\nTeacher Input:\n- This is an icon.\n- Many people recognise it.\n- Is it food, sport, or media?\n- Where have you seen this before?\n- Why do people remember this picture?\n- Choose one icon for your guide.\n- What does it show about the USA?\n\nPossible Child Response:\n- It is food.\n- It is sport.\n- I have seen this before.\n- Many people know it.\n- I choose basketball.\n- It shows popular culture.\n\n## 5. Suggested Games and Activities\n\n### Activity 1: Familiar or New?\n\n**Purpose:**  \nHelp children connect prior experience with new country exploration.\n\n**Materials:**  \nImage cards: hamburger, hot dog, popcorn, basketball, baseball, Hollywood sign, cartoon/superhero-style images, Coca-Cola-style product image, yellow taxi, Statue of Liberty.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare two floor mats: “I have seen this” and “New to me.”\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren choose image cards and place them on one of the two mats. Discuss which images many children know and which are new. The teacher introduces the idea that some pictures become widely recognised around the world.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nUse commercial products as cultural examples only. Avoid making the activity feel like brand promotion.\n\n### Activity 2: Icon Category Challenge\n\n**Purpose:**  \nStrengthen organisation and explanation using concrete categories.\n\n**Materials:**  \nIcon cards, category labels: Food, Sport, Film / Cartoon, City, Landmark, Art.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare a group table with category labels. Include a few cards that could fit more than one category.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren sort cards into categories, then choose one card and explain why it belongs there. For example: “Basketball is sport,” “Popcorn is food,” “Hollywood is film.” Stronger children can suggest two possible categories.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nK3 children can begin to understand “icon” as “a picture or thing many people recognise.” Keep the definition simple.\n\n### Activity 3: Choose One USA Icon Page\n\n**Purpose:**  \nPrepare an individual or group page for the final mini guide or museum.\n\n**Materials:**  \nBlank guide page templates, icon cards, drawing materials, glue, simple sentence frames.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare page templates with spaces for picture, name, category, and one sentence.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nEach child or group chooses one USA icon. They draw or paste the image, write or copy the name, select a category, and complete a short sentence with teacher support, such as “This is food,” “This is sport,” or “Many people know this.”\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nChildren do not need to write independently. Teacher-scribed explanations are acceptable.",
              "zh": "# 美国 · K3 · 第 2 课\n## 美国标志——食物、运动和流行文化\n\n## 1. 课程身份\n\n- 国家 / 地区：美国\n- 年级：K3\n- 课次：4 课中的第 2 课\n\n## 2. 课程重点\n\n幼儿调查来自食物、运动、电影、卡通和日常视觉文化的熟悉美国标志，并讨论为什么有些图像会被广泛认出。\n\n## 3. 学习目标\n\n幼儿将：\n\n- 识别和美国有关的食物、运动和流行文化图像；\n- 按类别和功能组织这些标志；\n- 比较\"哪些是熟悉的、哪些是新的\"，并挑一个标志作为美国指南或博物馆的内容。\n\n## 4. 教师语言\n\n教师输入：\n\n- This is an icon.\n- Many people recognise it.\n- Is it food, sport, or media?\n- Where have you seen this before?\n- Why do people remember this picture?\n- Choose one icon for your guide.\n- What does it show about the USA?\n\n幼儿可能回应：\n\n- It is food.\n- It is sport.\n- I have seen this before.\n- Many people know it.\n- I choose basketball.\n- It shows popular culture.\n\n## 5. 建议游戏与活动\n\n### 活动 1：熟悉还是新鲜？\n\n**目的：**\n帮助幼儿把\"已有的生活经验\"和\"新的国家探索\"连起来。\n\n**材料：**\n图片卡：汉堡、热狗、爆米花、篮球、棒球、好莱坞标志、卡通或超级英雄风格图像、可口可乐风格的产品图像、黄色出租车、自由女神像。\n\n**准备：**\n在地面铺两张垫子：\"我见过这个\"和\"对我来说新鲜的\"。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿选图片卡，放到其中一张垫上。讨论哪些图是很多孩子都认识的，哪些是新的。教师引入一个想法：有些图像会在全世界被认出来。\n\n**教师提示：**\n用商业产品只作为文化例子，不要让活动感觉像品牌宣传。\n\n### 活动 2：标志分类挑战\n\n**目的：**\n用具体类别加强组织与解释能力。\n\n**材料：**\n标志卡、类别标签：食物、运动、电影 / 卡通、城市、地标、艺术。\n\n**准备：**\n在小组桌上放好类别标签。故意放几张\"可以归到不止一个类别\"的卡。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿把卡分类，再挑一张卡解释它为什么属于这个类别。比如：\"Basketball is sport\"\"Popcorn is food\"\"Hollywood is film\"。能力较强的幼儿可以说出第二个可能的类别。\n\n**教师提示：**\nK3 幼儿可以开始把\"icon\"理解为\"很多人在很多人都会认出的图或物\"。定义保持简单。\n\n### 活动 3：选一个美国标志做一页\n\n**目的：**\n为最后的小指南或小博物馆准备一张个人或小组页。\n\n**材料：**\n空白的指南页模板、标志卡、画材、胶水、简单句型框架。\n\n**准备：**\n准备页模板，标好\"图、名字、类别、一句话\"几个区域。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n每位幼儿或每个小组选一个美国标志。可以画或贴上图像，写或抄下名字，选一个类别，并在教师支持下完成一句短句，比如 \"This is food\"\"This is sport\"\"Many people know this\"。\n\n**教师提示：**\n不要求幼儿独立书写。教师代写解释完全可以。"
            }
