            "markdown": {
              "en": "# USA · K3 · Lesson 3\n## Pop Art and Visual Communication\n\n## 1. Lesson Identity\n\n- Country / Place: USA\n- Grade: K3\n- Lesson: 3 of 4\n\n## 2. Lesson Focus\n\nChildren explore Pop Art-inspired visual communication by repeating, enlarging, recolouring, and arranging familiar images to make a strong visual message.\n\n## 3. Learning Objectives\n\nChildren will:\n- understand that repeated and colourful images can communicate strongly;\n- identify same/different, repetition, enlargement, and colour change in visual examples;\n- design a Pop Art-inspired page or poster using a USA-related icon and explain one design choice in simple language.\n\n## 4. Teacher Language\n\nTeacher Input:\n- The image repeats.\n- The colour changes.\n- This picture is big and bright.\n- What message does it give?\n- Choose one image.\n- Repeat it four times.\n- What did you change?\n- Tell us about your design.\n\nPossible Child Response:\n- I changed the colour.\n- I repeated the picture.\n- It is bright.\n- I chose a taxi.\n- My picture shows food.\n- Same picture, different colours.\n\n## 5. Suggested Games and Activities\n\n### Activity 1: Visual Message Detective\n\n**Purpose:**  \nHelp children notice how images can attract attention through repetition, colour, and size.\n\n**Materials:**  \nTeacher-made Pop Art-style examples using child-appropriate images: hamburger, taxi, basketball, star, building, drink bottle shape.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare two or three clear examples. Avoid overly complex or adult-oriented art discussion.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren look at the examples and identify what repeats, what changes, and what is big or bright. The teacher asks, “What do you notice?” “Which picture repeats?” “What colour changed?”\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nThis is not an art history lecture. Keep the focus on visual communication and design choices.\n\n### Activity 2: USA Pop Poster Design\n\n**Purpose:**  \nLet children create a designed output for the final USA display.\n\n**Materials:**  \nPoster paper or four-square templates, markers, coloured paper, stamps, icon templates, glue, scissors, repeated-image examples.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare image templates and sentence frames such as “I chose ___” and “I changed ___.”\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren choose one USA-related icon and repeat it across a page or poster. They change colour, background, size, or arrangement. Encourage them to make the image visually strong and easy to recognise.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nK3 children can make more intentional design choices than K1/K2. Encourage planning before sticking or colouring.\n\n### Activity 3: Design Choice Share\n\n**Purpose:**  \nPrepare children for final presentation by explaining one visual decision.\n\n**Materials:**  \nFinished posters, sentence cards, display wall.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare simple speaking frames:\n- I chose ___ .\n- I repeated ___ .\n- I changed ___ .\n- My picture shows ___ .\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren show their poster to a partner or small group and use one sentence frame to explain their design. Then they place the poster on the USA information wall or mini museum area.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nAccept incomplete speech and teacher-supported explanation. The goal is clear communication, not perfect language.",
              "zh": "# 美国 · K3 · 第 3 课\n## Pop Art 波普艺术和视觉传达\n\n## 1. 课程身份\n\n- 国家 / 地区：美国\n- 年级：K3\n- 课次：4 课中的第 3 课\n\n## 2. 课程重点\n\n幼儿通过重复、放大、换色和排列熟悉图像，探索波普艺术风格的视觉传达，做出一个\"有强烈视觉信号\"的作品。\n\n## 3. 学习目标\n\n幼儿将：\n\n- 理解重复和颜色鲜明的图像可以有很强的视觉传达效果；\n- 在视觉例子中识别相同 / 不同、重复、放大和颜色变化；\n- 围绕一个和美国有关的标志设计一张波普艺术风格页或海报，并用简单的话解释一个设计选择。\n\n## 4. 教师语言\n\n教师输入：\n\n- The image repeats.\n- The colour changes.\n- This picture is big and bright.\n- What message does it give?\n- Choose one image.\n- Repeat it four times.\n- What did you change?\n- Tell us about your design.\n\n幼儿可能回应：\n\n- I changed the colour.\n- I repeated the picture.\n- It is bright.\n- I chose a taxi.\n- My picture shows food.\n- Same picture, different colours.\n\n## 5. 建议游戏与活动\n\n### 活动 1：视觉信号小侦探\n\n**目的：**\n帮助幼儿注意\"图像通过重复、颜色和大小吸引注意力\"。\n\n**材料：**\n教师自制的波普艺术风格样张，用适合幼儿的图像：汉堡、出租车、篮球、星星、建筑、饮料瓶形状。\n\n**准备：**\n准备 2–3 张清晰的样张。避免太复杂或太成人化的艺术讨论。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿看样张，找出\"哪里在重复、哪里在变化、什么是大而明亮的\"。教师问：\"What do you notice?\"\"Which picture repeats?\"\"What colour changed?\"。\n\n**教师提示：**\n这不是艺术史讲座。重点是\"视觉传达\"和\"设计选择\"。\n\n### 活动 2：美国波普海报设计\n\n**目的：**\n让幼儿为最终的美国展示做出一件有设计感的输出。\n\n**材料：**\n海报纸或四格模板、马克笔、彩色纸、印章、标志模板、胶水、剪刀、重复图像样例。\n\n**准备：**\n准备图像模板和句型框架，比如\"I chose ___\"\"I changed ___\"。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿选一个和美国有关的标志，在一页纸或一张海报上重复它。可以换颜色、背景、大小或排列方式。鼓励他们把图像做得视觉上强、容易认。\n\n**教师提示：**\nK3 幼儿可以做出比 K1 / K2 更有意图的设计选择。鼓励他们在贴或涂之前先想一下。\n\n### 活动 3：分享一个设计选择\n\n**目的：**\n用\"解释一个视觉决定\"为最后的展示做准备。\n\n**材料：**\n完成的海报、句型卡、展示墙。\n\n**准备：**\n准备简单说话框架：\n- I chose ___ .\n- I repeated ___ .\n- I changed ___ .\n- My picture shows ___ .\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿向同伴或小组展示自己的海报，用其中一个句型解释自己的设计。然后把海报贴到美国信息墙或小博物馆区。\n\n**教师提示：**\n可以接受说不完整的话或教师支持的解释。重点是\"讲清楚\"，不是\"讲漂亮\"。"
            }
