            "number": 3,
            "markdown": {
              "en": "# Kenya · K1 · Lesson 3\n## Colours, Patterns and Textures\n\n## 1. Lesson Identity\n\n- Country / Place: Kenya\n- Grade: K1\n- Lesson: 3 of 4\n\n## 2. Lesson Focus\n\nChildren explore Kenya through animal patterns, grassland colours, and tactile materials. They notice stripes, spots, rough, smooth, soft, brown, yellow, green, and black-and-white contrasts, then create a simple pattern collage.\n\n## 3. Learning Objectives\n\nChildren will:\n- notice visible patterns such as stripes and spots on animal images;\n- explore colour and texture materials through touching, choosing, and arranging;\n- create a simple Kenya-inspired collage with teacher support.\n\n## 4. Teacher Language\n\nTeacher Input:\n- I see stripes.\n- I see spots.\n- Touch gently. Is it soft or rough?\n- Choose a colour.\n- Put it here.\n\nPossible Child Response:\n- stripes / spots\n- soft / rough\n- black / white / yellow / brown / green\n- choosing, touching, placing, gluing\n\n## 5. Suggested Games and Activities\n\n### Activity 1: Stripes and Spots Search\n\n**Purpose:**  \nTo help children notice animal patterns visually.\n\n**Materials:**  \nZebra, giraffe, leopard, and other animal images; pattern cards with stripes and spots.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPlace animal images and simple pattern cards on a table or wall.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren look for stripes and spots. They place a stripe card near a zebra image and a spot card near a giraffe or leopard image. The teacher repeats simple language: “stripes,” “spots,” “same,” “look.”\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nKeep the set small. Too many animal patterns will make the task visually noisy for K1.\n\n### Activity 2: Texture Touch Basket\n\n**Purpose:**  \nTo give children a sensory entry into the Kenya theme.\n\n**Materials:**  \nFabric scraps, felt, textured paper, smooth card, brown/yellow/green paper, baskets.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare baskets with safe textures and colours. Avoid small loose pieces that may be choking hazards.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren touch and choose materials. The teacher names simple sensory qualities: soft, rough, smooth. Children sort materials into colour groups or place favourite textures on a mat.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nThis is a sensory activity, not an art product yet. Allow exploration before gluing.\n\n### Activity 3: Kenya Pattern Collage\n\n**Purpose:**  \nTo create a child-made visual piece for the Kenya display.\n\n**Materials:**  \nA4 or A3 paper, pre-cut strips, circles or spots, textured paper, glue sticks, animal outline templates if needed.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare simple collage materials in limited colours: black, white, yellow, brown, green.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren choose strips, spots, and textures to arrange on paper. They may make a zebra pattern, giraffe spots, or an abstract grassland pattern. The teacher supports placement and gluing.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nAvoid correcting children toward realistic animal patterns. The goal is noticing and making, not accurate representation.",
              "zh": "# 肯尼亚 · K1 · 第 3 课\n## 颜色、图案和触感\n\n## 1. 课程身份\n\n- 国家 / 地区：肯尼亚\n- 年级：K1\n- 课次：4 课中的第 3 课\n\n## 2. 课程重点\n\n幼儿通过动物图案、草原颜色和有质感的材料来探索肯尼亚。他们注意条纹、斑点、粗糙、光滑、柔软、棕色、黄色、绿色，以及黑白对比，然后做一幅简单的图案拼贴。\n\n## 3. 学习目标\n\n幼儿将：\n\n- 注意到动物图片上看得见的图案，比如条纹和斑点；\n- 通过触摸、选择和摆放来探索颜色和质感材料；\n- 在教师支持下，做一幅简单的、受肯尼亚启发的拼贴。\n\n## 4. 教师语言\n\n教师输入：\n\n- I see stripes.\n- I see spots.\n- Touch gently. Is it soft or rough?\n- Choose a colour.\n- Put it here.\n\n幼儿可能回应：\n\n- stripes / spots\n- soft / rough\n- black / white / yellow / brown / green\n- choosing, touching, placing, gluing\n\n## 5. 建议游戏与活动\n\n### 活动 1：找条纹，找斑点\n\n**目的：**\n帮助幼儿在视觉上注意动物的图案。\n\n**材料：**\n斑马、长颈鹿、豹子等动物图片；印有条纹和斑点的图案卡。\n\n**准备：**\n把动物图片和简单图案卡放在桌上或墙上。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿找条纹和斑点。把一张条纹卡放到斑马图旁，把一张斑点卡放到长颈鹿或豹子图旁。教师重复简单语言：\"stripes\"\"spots\"\"same\"\"look\"。\n\n**教师提示：**\n整套材料保持少量。图案太多会让 K1 觉得视觉过载。\n\n### 活动 2：触感小篮\n\n**目的：**\n给幼儿一个\"用身体感觉\"进入肯尼亚主题的机会。\n\n**材料：**\n布头、毛毡、有质感的纸、光滑卡纸、棕 / 黄 / 绿色纸、篮子。\n\n**准备：**\n把安全、有质感的材料分到几个篮子里。避免容易脱落、可能被误吞的小零件。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿摸一摸、选一选。教师说出简单的质感词：soft、rough、smooth。幼儿按颜色分组，或者把自己最喜欢的质感放到垫子上。\n\n**教师提示：**\n这是\"触感探索\"环节，还没到做作品的阶段。允许幼儿先玩一玩，再开始粘贴。\n\n### 活动 3：肯尼亚图案拼贴\n\n**目的：**\n为肯尼亚展示做出一件幼儿自己做的小视觉作品。\n\n**材料：**\nA4 或 A3 纸、预剪好的纸条、圆点或斑点、有质感的纸、胶棒、如有需要可以准备动物轮廓模板。\n\n**准备：**\n准备简单的拼贴材料，颜色限制在：黑、白、黄、棕、绿。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿选纸条、斑点、质感纸，在纸上摆放。可以做斑马图案、长颈鹿斑点，或一个抽象的草原图案。教师在摆放和粘贴时给支持。\n\n**教师提示：**\n不要把幼儿往\"画得逼真\"的方向纠正。重点是\"注意到了\"和\"做出来了\"，不是准确还原。"
            }
