            "markdown": {
              "en": "# Germany · K1 · Lesson 2\n## Trains, Tracks and Stations\n\n## 1. Lesson Identity\n\n- Country / Place: Germany\n- Grade: K1\n- Lesson: 2 of 4\n\n## 2. Lesson Focus\n\nChildren explore Germany through trains, tracks, and stations. The focus is on joining pieces, following a route, moving trains safely, and noticing long/short, together/apart, and in/out through play.\n\n## 3. Learning Objectives\n\nChildren will:\n- notice trains, tracks, stations, and tunnels as concrete transport elements;\n- participate in building or using a simple train route with adult support;\n- respond to route language through placing, joining, moving, waiting, or single words.\n\n## 4. Teacher Language\n\nTeacher Input:\n- This is a train.\n- Put the train on the track.\n- Join the tracks together.\n- The train goes to the station.\n- Wait. Now go.\n\nPossible Child Response:\n- train / track / station / tunnel\n- go / stop / long\n- joining, placing, moving, waiting\n\n## 5. Suggested Games and Activities\n\n### Activity 1: Track Builders\n\n**Purpose:**  \nTo support hand-eye coordination and shared construction through train-track play.\n\n**Materials:**  \nWooden or plastic train tracks, toy trains, small station blocks, tunnel pieces.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPlace track pieces in baskets and prepare a simple example track for reference.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nInvite children to help join track pieces. The teacher supports by holding pieces steady and naming actions: join, turn, long, short. Once a route is ready, children move trains around the track.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nDo not require all children to build a complete route. Partial joining and placing are valid participation.\n\n### Activity 2: Station Stop Game\n\n**Purpose:**  \nTo practise controlled movement and waiting.\n\n**Materials:**  \nToy train, station cards or blocks, small figures, stop/go cards.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nSet up two or three stations along the track.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren move the train from station to station. At each station, they stop, place a small figure, or wave. The teacher uses simple prompts: “Stop at the station,” “People get in,” “Train goes.”\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nKeep the rhythm predictable. This helps K1 children join without needing much verbal output.\n\n### Activity 3: Tunnel and Bridge Train Play\n\n**Purpose:**  \nTo let children notice over, under, in, and out through train movement.\n\n**Materials:**  \nBlocks, cardboard tunnels, low bridge pieces, train tracks, toy trains.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nBuild one tunnel and one low bridge along the track.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nInvite children to send the train through the tunnel and under or over the bridge depending on the setup. Children can add more blocks to make the tunnel longer.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nUse prepositions as exposure only. Children can respond by moving the train correctly.",
              "zh": "# 德国 · K1 · 第 2 课\n## 火车、轨道和车站\n\n## 1. 课程身份\n\n- 国家 / 地区：德国\n- 年级：K1\n- 课次：4 课中的第 2 课\n\n## 2. 课程重点\n\n幼儿通过火车、轨道和车站认识德国。重点是拼装、跟着路线走、安全地开小火车，并在玩中注意长 / 短、一起 / 分开、进 / 出。\n\n## 3. 学习目标\n\n幼儿将：\n\n- 注意到火车、轨道、车站、隧道这些具体的交通元素；\n- 在成人支持下，参与搭建或使用一条简单的火车路线；\n- 通过放、拼、推、等待或一个词对\"路线语言\"做出回应。\n\n## 4. 教师语言\n\n教师输入：\n\n- This is a train.\n- Put the train on the track.\n- Join the tracks together.\n- The train goes to the station.\n- Wait. Now go.\n\n幼儿可能回应：\n\n- train / track / station / tunnel\n- go / stop / long\n- joining, placing, moving, waiting\n\n## 5. 建议游戏与活动\n\n### 活动 1：轨道搭建师\n\n**目的：**\n用火车轨道游戏支持手眼协调和合作搭建。\n\n**材料：**\n木质或塑料火车轨道、玩具小火车、小车站积木、隧道片。\n\n**准备：**\n把轨道片放在几个篮子里，预先搭好一条示范轨道做参考。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n请幼儿一起帮忙拼接轨道。教师帮忙固定，并说出动作词：join、turn、long、short。路线搭好后，幼儿用小火车沿线开。\n\n**教师提示：**\n不要求每位幼儿都搭完整条路线。拼一部分、放一放、搭一节，都是有效的参与。\n\n### 活动 2：车站停靠游戏\n\n**目的：**\n练习受控的\"动\"和\"等\"。\n\n**材料：**\n玩具小火车、车站卡或积木、小人偶、停 / 走卡。\n\n**准备：**\n在轨道沿线设两到三个车站。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿把火车从一个车站开到另一个车站。每到一站就停一下，放上小人偶或挥挥手。教师用简单提示：\"Stop at the station\"\"People get in\"\"Train goes\"。\n\n**教师提示：**\n节奏保持可预期。这样 K1 幼儿不需要太多语言就能加入。\n\n### 活动 3：隧道和桥的火车游戏\n\n**目的：**\n让幼儿在开火车时注意到\"上、下、进、出\"。\n\n**材料：**\n积木、纸板隧道、低矮的桥片、火车轨道、玩具小火车。\n\n**准备：**\n在轨道上搭一个隧道和一座低矮的桥。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n请幼儿把火车开过隧道，并根据搭建的方式从桥上或桥下通过。幼儿可以继续加积木，把隧道加长。\n\n**教师提示：**\n\"上下进出\"只作为语言接触。幼儿能正确地开火车通过，就是有效的回应。"
            }
