            "markdown": {
              "en": "# Germany · K2 · Lesson 2\n## Forests, Animals and Small Towns\n\n## 1. Lesson Identity\n\n- Country / Place: Germany\n- Grade: K2\n- Lesson: 2 of 4\n\n## 2. Lesson Focus\n\nChildren explore Germany through forests and small towns. The lesson focuses on connections: forests have trees and animals; towns have houses, paths, and people; some places are close to nature. Children sort, match, and build a forest-town relationship.\n\n## 3. Learning Objectives\n\nChildren will:\n- identify and sort simple forest and town elements such as trees, animals, houses, paths, and people;\n- connect animals and objects to suitable places in a forest-town scene;\n- compare natural and built elements using simple same/different language.\n\n## 4. Teacher Language\n\nTeacher Input:\n- Is this from the forest or the town?\n- Trees are in the forest.\n- Houses are in the town.\n- The path connects the forest and the town.\n- What is natural? What is built?\n\nPossible Child Response:\n- forest / town / tree / house / path / animal\n- same / different\n- in the forest / in the town / near the trees\n\n## 5. Suggested Games and Activities\n\n### Activity 1: Forest or Town Sort\n\n**Purpose:**  \nTo help children classify natural and built elements.\n\n**Materials:**  \nPicture cards or objects: trees, animals, mushrooms, houses, roofs, roads, people, shops, paths.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nSet up two large areas labelled with pictures: forest and town.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren sort cards into forest or town. For objects that can connect both areas, such as paths or people, the teacher invites children to place them between the two areas.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nDo not force one correct answer for every card. Some cards can support discussion.\n\n### Activity 2: Build a Forest-Town Edge\n\n**Purpose:**  \nTo make the relationship between nature and settlement visible.\n\n**Materials:**  \nBlocks, green fabric, paper trees, house pieces, road strips, path markers, small animals.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nPrepare a large base with one side for forest and one side for town.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nChildren build trees and animals on one side, houses and roads on the other, then add paths to connect them. Ask where people might walk and where animals might stay.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nKeep animal content simple and non-threatening. Focus on place relationships.\n\n### Activity 3: Same and Different Picture Talk\n\n**Purpose:**  \nTo support visual comparison using real or illustrated Germany images.\n\n**Materials:**  \nImages of German forests, small towns, timber-style houses, paths, and trees.\n\n**Preparation:**  \nChoose four to six clear images with obvious visual contrasts.\n\n**How to Play / Do:**  \nShow two images at a time. Children identify what is the same and what is different: trees, houses, roads, roofs, colours, animals, people.\n\n**Teacher Notes:**  \nThis should remain conversational. One-word responses are enough.",
              "zh": "# 德国 · K2 · 第 2 课\n## 森林、动物和小镇\n\n## 1. 课程身份\n\n- 国家 / 地区：德国\n- 年级：K2\n- 课次：4 课中的第 2 课\n\n## 2. 课程重点\n\n幼儿通过森林和小镇认识德国。本课重点是\"联系\"：森林有树和动物；小镇有房子、小路、人；有些地方紧挨着自然。幼儿通过分类、匹配和搭建来理解\"森林和小镇\"的关系。\n\n## 3. 学习目标\n\n幼儿将：\n\n- 识别并分类简单的森林和城镇元素：树、动物、房子、小路、人；\n- 把动物和物品放到森林—小镇场景里合适的位置；\n- 用简单的\"相同 / 不同\"语言比较自然元素和人造元素。\n\n## 4. 教师语言\n\n教师输入：\n\n- Is this from the forest or the town?\n- Trees are in the forest.\n- Houses are in the town.\n- The path connects the forest and the town.\n- What is natural? What is built?\n\n幼儿可能回应：\n\n- forest / town / tree / house / path / animal\n- same / different\n- in the forest / in the town / near the trees\n\n## 5. 建议游戏与活动\n\n### 活动 1：森林还是小镇？\n\n**目的：**\n帮助幼儿分类\"自然的\"和\"人造的\"元素。\n\n**材料：**\n图片卡或实物：树、动物、蘑菇、房子、屋顶、马路、人、店铺、小路。\n\n**准备：**\n设两个大区，分别用图片标\"森林\"和\"小镇\"。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿把卡片分到\"森林\"或\"小镇\"。对于\"两边都能放\"的卡（比如小路、人），教师可以请幼儿把它放到两个区的中间。\n\n**教师提示：**\n不要给每张卡都强求一个唯一正确答案。有的卡正好可以引出讨论。\n\n### 活动 2：搭一片\"森林—小镇\"边界\n\n**目的：**\n让\"自然—聚落\"的关系变得看得见。\n\n**材料：**\n积木、绿色布、纸树、房子片、马路片、小路标记、小动物。\n\n**准备：**\n准备一张大底板，一边是\"森林\"，一边是\"小镇\"。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n幼儿一边搭树和动物，另一边搭房子和马路，再用小路把它们连起来。问：\"人会走哪里？动物会待在哪里？\"\n\n**教师提示：**\n动物内容保持简单、不可怕。重点放在\"地点之间的关系\"。\n\n### 活动 3：相同和不同——看图说话\n\n**目的：**\n用真实或写实的德国图片支持视觉比较。\n\n**材料：**\n德国森林、小镇、木屋、小路、树的图片。\n\n**准备：**\n选 4–6 张图片，要有明显对比。\n\n**玩法 / 做法：**\n一次出示两张图。幼儿说出相同和不同：树、房子、马路、屋顶、颜色、动物、人。\n\n**教师提示：**\n保持对话式。说一个词就够了。"
            }
